      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m Dr. ____. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Hello, Doctor. Well, my daughter wanted me to come talk to you because... well, she says I never sit still, and I suppose she's right. I feel like I’m always up and moving. Even on a quiet day when I'm supposed to be relaxing, I’m bouncing from the garden club list to my knitting bag to digging out old travel papers before I’ve really finished any one thing. \n\nWhich reminds me, I was looking through those travel papers because I wanted to find the itinerary from our Alaska cruise. We went a few years ago and it was just spectacular. Have you ever been? They served this baked Alaska dessert on the ship, which I always thought was a bit of a cliché, but it was actually delicious. I tried to make it at home once for my grandson's birthday, but the meringue didn't set right at all. I think it was too humid that day, or maybe my oven runs a little hot. I've been meaning to have the repairman look at it, but he charges a fortune just to come out to the house... \n\nI'm sorry, what was I saying? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yes, just always on the go, I suppose.",
