    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you noticed any recent problems with your memory?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Memory? Oh, well, no, I wouldn't say my memory is bad. I mean, I can remember all sorts of things. Just the other day, I was telling my daughter about the time we went to the state fair when she was a little girl. She must have been about seven, maybe eight? She had this bright pink cotton candy, and it got all in her hair. It was a nightmare to wash out, let me tell you. We had to use that special shampoo, the one in the yellow bottle... what was it called? Johnson's, I think. Do they still make that? I haven't bought baby shampoo in ages. \n\nMy grandson uses this fancy organic stuff now that costs an arm and a leg. His mother buys it online. I tried to order some things online once, some knitting yarn, but the website was so confusing. All these buttons and pop-ups. I ended up calling the company instead. The woman on the phone was very nice, though. She lived in Ohio, and we had a lovely chat about the weather. It was snowing there, but here it was just raining. I hate the rain, it makes my knees ache. \n\nBut anyway, no, my memory is fine. I just... I just have a lot on my mind, I suppose.",
